IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`
IMPORT `coa24-officers`
IMPORT `coa24-penalty`
IMPORT `coa24-identity`
IMPORT `coa24-acsp`

-- coa24-tests-acsp.l4: tests for ss 1098A to 1098H (coa24-acsp.l4). Expected values were decided from the text before the
-- run. The pounds are test figures that stand for nothing.

§ `Fixtures`

`the test amounts` MEANS `s 1125 amounts the Act leaves to other instruments` WITH
    `s 1125 level 1 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 100
    `s 1125 level 2 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 200
    `s 1125 level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 300
    `s 1125 level 4 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 400
    `s 1125 level 5 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 500
    `s 1125 the statutory maximum, in pounds` IS 1000

`a director who permitted the contravention` MEANS `s 1121(3) conduct of the officer` WITH
    `s 1121(3) authorises or permits` IS TRUE
    `s 1121(3) participates in` IS FALSE
    `s 1121(3) fails to take all reasonable steps to prevent` IS FALSE

`a director who did nothing wrong` MEANS `s 1121(3) conduct of the officer` WITH
    `s 1121(3) authorises or permits` IS FALSE
    `s 1121(3) participates in` IS FALSE
    `s 1121(3) fails to take all reasonable steps to prevent` IS FALSE

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A BOOLEAN, e IS A BOOLEAN, f IS A BOOLEAN, g IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 1098C(1) particulars supplied for a firm`
`a firm's particulars with the seven items` MEANS `s 1098C(1) particulars supplied for a firm` WITH
    `s 1098C(1)(a) firm name` IS a
    `s 1098C(1)(b) principal office` IS b
    `s 1098C(1)(c) a service address` IS c
    `s 1098C(1)(d) an email address` IS d
    `s 1098C(1)(e) the legal form of the firm and the law by which it is governed` IS e
    `s 1098C(1)(ea) any registration number allocated to the firm under regulation 54 or 55 of the Money Laundering Regulations` IS f
    `s 1098C(1)(f) if applicable, any other register in which it is entered (including details of the state) and its registration number in that register` IS g

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A BOOLEAN, e IS A BOOLEAN, f IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 1098C(2) particulars supplied for an individual`
`an individual's particulars with the six items` MEANS `s 1098C(2) particulars supplied for an individual` WITH
    `s 1098C(2)(a) nationality` IS a
    `s 1098C(2)(a) date of birth` IS b
    `s 1098C(2)(b) a service address` IS c
    `s 1098C(2)(c) an email address` IS d
    `s 1098C(2)(d) the part of the United Kingdom in which the person is usually resident or, if usually resident outside the United Kingdom, that country or state` IS e
    `s 1098C(2)(e) any registration number allocated to the individual under regulation 54 or 55 of the Money Laundering Regulations` IS f

§ `Tests for s 1098A`

-- Means a person whose application has been granted, who has not since ceased, and whose status is not suspended.
#ASSERT `s 1098A the person is an authorised corporate service provider` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098A the person is an authorised corporate service provider` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1098A the person is an authorised corporate service provider` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1098A the person is an authorised corporate service provider` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1098A the person is an authorised corporate service provider` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests for s 1098B`

-- (1): (a) a relevant person, (b) for an individual, identity verified, (c) any other requirements met.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 1098B(1) the person may apply to become an authorised corporate service provider` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE; name-test sweep (fork F19): the function is named for a grant or a power ("A person may apply ... if"), its gate is "if", and a failed "if" gate answers NOTHING, not the text's own no; the other reading, JUST FALSE, is in the fork register
#ASSERT `s 1098B(1) the person may apply to become an authorised corporate service provider` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1098B(1) the person may apply to become an authorised corporate service provider` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 1098B(1) the person may apply to become an authorised corporate service provider` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE; name-test sweep (fork F19): the function is named for a grant or a power ("A person may apply ... if"), its gate is "if", and a failed "if" gate answers NOTHING, not the text's own no; the other reading, JUST FALSE, is in the fork register
#ASSERT `s 1098B(1) the person may apply to become an authorised corporate service provider` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A firm: paragraph (b) speaks only "in the case of an individual", so the identity answer is not read.
#ASSERT `s 1098B(1) the person may apply to become an authorised corporate service provider` TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098B(1) the person may apply to become an authorised corporate service provider` TRUE FALSE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098B(1) the person may apply to become an authorised corporate service provider` TRUE TRUE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 1098B(1) the person may apply to become an authorised corporate service provider` TRUE FALSE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE; name-test sweep (fork F19): the function is named for a grant or a power ("A person may apply ... if"), its gate is "if", and a failed "if" gate answers NOTHING, not the text's own no; the other reading, JUST FALSE, is in the fork register
#ASSERT `s 1098B(1) the person may apply to become an authorised corporate service provider` TRUE FALSE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1098B(1) the person may apply to become an authorised corporate service provider` TRUE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 1098B(1) the person may apply to become an authorised corporate service provider` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE; name-test sweep (fork F19): the function is named for a grant or a power ("A person may apply ... if"), its gate is "if", and a failed "if" gate answers NOTHING, not the text's own no; the other reading, JUST FALSE, is in the fork register
#ASSERT `s 1098B(1) the person may apply to become an authorised corporate service provider` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2): name of supervisory authority, required information, and for an individual a statement of verified identity.
#ASSERT `s 1098B(2) the application meets the requirement of s 1098B(2)` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098B(2) the application meets the requirement of s 1098B(2)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098B(2) the application meets the requirement of s 1098B(2)` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1098B(2) the application meets the requirement of s 1098B(2)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1098B(2) the application meets the requirement of s 1098B(2)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `s 1098B(3) the registrar must check with the supervisory authority` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098B(3) the registrar must check with the supervisory authority` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (5): must refuse if it appears the applicant is not a fit and proper person.
#ASSERT `s 1098B(5) the registrar must refuse the application` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098B(5) the registrar must refuse the application` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (4): must grant if (a) confirmed, (b) identity satisfied for an individual, (c) other conditions met, (d) not required to refuse.
#ASSERT `s 1098B(4) the registrar must grant the application` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098B(4) the registrar must grant the application` TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098B(4) the registrar must grant the application` FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1098B(4) the registrar must grant the application` TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (d): the registrar is required by subsection (5) to refuse, so it is not required to grant.
#ASSERT `s 1098B(4) the registrar must grant the application` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1098B(4) the registrar must grant the application` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1098B(4) the registrar must grant the application` TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1098B(4) the registrar must grant the application` TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `s 1098B(8) the Money Laundering Regulations` EQUALS "the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 (S.I. 2017/692)"
#ASSERT `s 1098B(8) the person is supervised by the supervisory authority` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098B(8) the person is supervised by the supervisory authority` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1098B(8) the authority is a supervisory authority` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098B(8) the authority is a supervisory authority` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

