#ASSERT `s 1098C(4A) the meaning of "Money Laundering Regulations"` EQUALS `s 1098B(8) the Money Laundering Regulations`

§ `Tests for s 1098D`

-- The table: company | director.
#ASSERT `s 1098D table the position is a relevant officer of the firm` `s 1098D a company` FALSE `s 1098D a director` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098D table the position is a relevant officer of the firm` `s 1098D a company` FALSE `s 1098D a member of the body` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A body corporate other than a company: where managed by its members, a member; in any other case, an officer corresponding to a director.
#ASSERT `s 1098D table the position is a relevant officer of the firm` `s 1098D a body corporate other than a company` TRUE `s 1098D a member of the body` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098D table the position is a relevant officer of the firm` `s 1098D a body corporate other than a company` TRUE `s 1098D an officer of the body whose functions correspond to that of a director of a company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1098D table the position is a relevant officer of the firm` `s 1098D a body corporate other than a company` FALSE `s 1098D an officer of the body whose functions correspond to that of a director of a company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098D table the position is a relevant officer of the firm` `s 1098D a body corporate other than a company` FALSE `s 1098D a member of the body` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A partnership: a limited partnership, a general partner; any other partnership, a member.
#ASSERT `s 1098D table the position is a relevant officer of the firm` `s 1098D a limited partnership` FALSE `s 1098D a general partner as defined by section 3 of the Limited Partnerships Act 1907` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098D table the position is a relevant officer of the firm` `s 1098D a limited partnership` FALSE `s 1098D a member of the partnership` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1098D table the position is a relevant officer of the firm` `s 1098D a partnership other than a limited partnership` FALSE `s 1098D a member of the partnership` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098D table the position is a relevant officer of the firm` `s 1098D a partnership other than a limited partnership` FALSE `s 1098D a general partner as defined by section 3 of the Limited Partnerships Act 1907` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An unincorporated body other than a partnership: where managed by its members, a member; in any other case, a member of the governing body.
#ASSERT `s 1098D table the position is a relevant officer of the firm` `s 1098D an unincorporated body other than a partnership` TRUE `s 1098D a member of the body` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098D table the position is a relevant officer of the firm` `s 1098D an unincorporated body other than a partnership` TRUE `s 1098D a member of the governing body` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1098D table the position is a relevant officer of the firm` `s 1098D an unincorporated body other than a partnership` FALSE `s 1098D a member of the governing body` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098D table the position is a relevant officer of the firm` `s 1098D an unincorporated body other than a partnership` FALSE `s 1098D a member of the body` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (a) and (b): delivered by a relevant officer who is an individual, with a statement confirming their status.
#ASSERT `s 1098D the application meets the delivery requirements of s 1098D` `s 1098D a company` FALSE `s 1098D a director` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098D the application meets the delivery requirements of s 1098D` `s 1098D a company` FALSE `s 1098D a director` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1098D the application meets the delivery requirements of s 1098D` `s 1098D a company` FALSE `s 1098D a director` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1098D the application meets the delivery requirements of s 1098D` `s 1098D a company` FALSE `s 1098D another position` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1098D the application meets the delivery requirements of s 1098D` `s 1098D a limited partnership` FALSE `s 1098D a general partner as defined by section 3 of the Limited Partnerships Act 1907` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Tests for s 1098E`

-- (1): 14 days beginning with the day of the change: change on 1 March 2026, last day 14 March 2026.
#ASSERT `s 1098E(1)-(2) the last day for notifying the registrar of the change` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (Date 14 3 2026)
-- (2): where the change results from an agreement under regulation 7(2), it counts from the day the authority notifies or publishes (10 March 2026): last day 23 March 2026.
#ASSERT `s 1098E(1)-(2) the last day for notifying the registrar of the change` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 23 3 2026)
-- Not yet notified or published: no change is treated as having occurred, so no period runs.
#ASSERT `s 1098E(1)-(2) the last day for notifying the registrar of the change` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2) the "until" bar: before 10 March 2026 the change cannot yet be treated as having occurred; from that day it can.
#ASSERT `s 1098E(2) the change cannot yet be treated as having occurred` TRUE (Date 9 3 2026) (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098E(2) the change cannot yet be treated as having occurred` TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1098E(2) the change cannot yet be treated as having occurred` TRUE (Date 11 3 2026) (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1098E(2) the change cannot yet be treated as having occurred` TRUE (Date 11 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098E(2) the change cannot yet be treated as having occurred` FALSE (Date 11 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- (3): the offence needs a provider, a failure to notify in time, and no reasonable excuse.
#ASSERT `s 1098E(3) the person commits an offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098E(3) the person commits an offence` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1098E(3) the person commits an offence` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1098E(3) the person commits an offence` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (1)-(3) with dates. A change on 1 March 2026, no agreement; the last day is 14 March 2026.
#ASSERT `s 1098E(1)-(3) the person commits an offence by failing to notify the registrar in time` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (JUST (Date 14 3 2026)) (Date 30 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1098E(1)-(3) the person commits an offence by failing to notify the registrar in time` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (JUST (Date 15 3 2026)) (Date 30 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098E(1)-(3) the person commits an offence by failing to notify the registrar in time` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING NOTHING (Date 14 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1098E(1)-(3) the person commits an offence by failing to notify the registrar in time` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING NOTHING (Date 15 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A reasonable excuse takes the case out of the offence as the text is worded.
#ASSERT `s 1098E(1)-(3) the person commits an offence by failing to notify the registrar in time` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING NOTHING (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not an authorised corporate service provider: the duty is not theirs.
#ASSERT `s 1098E(1)-(3) the person commits an offence by failing to notify the registrar in time` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING NOTHING (Date 15 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- An agreement under regulation 7(2): the authority notified on 10 March 2026, so the last day is 23 March 2026.
#ASSERT `s 1098E(1)-(3) the person commits an offence by failing to notify the registrar in time` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) (JUST (Date 23 3 2026)) (Date 30 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1098E(1)-(3) the person commits an offence by failing to notify the registrar in time` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) (JUST (Date 24 3 2026)) (Date 30 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098E(1)-(3) the person commits an offence by failing to notify the registrar in time` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING NOTHING (Date 30 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (4): where the offence is committed by a firm every officer who is in default also commits it.
#ASSERT `s 1098E(4) the officer of the firm who is in default also commits the offence` `a company registered under the Companies Act 2006` (JUST TRUE) `s 1121(2)(a) a director` `a director who permitted the contravention` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098E(4) the officer of the firm who is in default also commits the offence` `a company registered under the Companies Act 2006` (JUST TRUE) `s 1121(2)(a) a director` `a director who did nothing wrong` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1098E(4) the officer of the firm who is in default also commits the offence` `a partnership` (JUST TRUE) `s 1121(2)(a) a director` `a director who permitted the contravention` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098E(4) the officer of the firm who is in default also commits the offence` `a company registered under the Companies Act 2006` NOTHING `s 1121(2)(a) a director` `a director who permitted the contravention` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Committed by an individual, not a firm: subsection (4) speaks only of a firm.
#ASSERT `s 1098E(4) the officer of the firm who is in default also commits the offence` `an individual` (JUST TRUE) `s 1121(2)(a) a director` `a director who permitted the contravention` EQUALS NOTHING

-- (5): on summary conviction, England and Wales a fine; Scotland or Northern Ireland a fine not exceeding level 5 and a daily default fine of one-tenth of level 5.
#ASSERT `s 1098E(5) the punishment on summary conviction` `England and Wales` EQUALS Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING, `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING, `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1098E(5) the punishment on summary conviction` Scotland EQUALS Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Scotland`, `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING, `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1), `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 0.1), `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1098E(5) the punishment on summary conviction` `Northern Ireland` EQUALS Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING, `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1), `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 0.1), `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE
-- Measured with s 1125: a second conviction in Scotland, 3 days of continued contravention: one-tenth of level 5 (test figure 500) is 50 a day, so 150.
#ASSERT `s 1125(2) the most the person can be fined on this conviction, in pounds` (`s 1098E(5) the punishment on summary conviction` Scotland) TRUE 3 `the test amounts` EQUALS JUST 150
-- England and Wales has no daily default fine, so s 1125 does not speak.
#ASSERT `s 1125(2) the most the person can be fined on this conviction, in pounds` (`s 1098E(5) the punishment on summary conviction` `England and Wales`) TRUE 3 `the test amounts` EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 1098E(6) the section that gives the meaning of "Money Laundering Regulations" and "supervisory authority"` EQUALS "section 1098B(8)"

-- The duty of subsection (1) as a regulative rule: day 0 is the day of the change. Notified on day 13 (the 14th day): FULFILLED.
-- Notified on day 14: late, BREACH. Never notified: BREACH. (Traces are read from the run; a DEONTIC cannot be compared in #ASSERT.)
#TRACE `s 1098E(1) the provider's duty to notify the registrar of the change` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 1098E(1) the authorised corporate service provider` DOES `s 1098E(1) notify the registrar of the change in supervisory authority` AT 13

#TRACE `s 1098E(1) the provider's duty to notify the registrar of the change` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 1098E(1) the authorised corporate service provider` DOES `s 1098E(1) notify the registrar of the change in supervisory authority` AT 14

#TRACE `s 1098E(1) the provider's duty to notify the registrar of the change` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 14)

§ `Tests for ss 1098F, 1098G and 1098H`

#ASSERT `s 1098F(1) the person ceases to be an authorised corporate service provider` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098F(1) the person ceases to be an authorised corporate service provider` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1098F(6) the section that gives the meaning of "Money Laundering Regulations"` EQUALS "section 1098B(8)"

-- s 1098G(5): the same scale as s 1098E(5), stated separately in the text.
#ASSERT `s 1098G(5) the punishment the regulations must provide for an offence` `England and Wales` EQUALS `s 1098E(5) the punishment on summary conviction` `England and Wales`
#ASSERT `s 1098G(5) the punishment the regulations must provide for an offence` Scotland EQUALS `s 1098E(5) the punishment on summary conviction` Scotland
#ASSERT `s 1098G(5) the punishment the regulations must provide for an offence` `Northern Ireland` EQUALS `s 1098E(5) the punishment on summary conviction` `Northern Ireland`

#ASSERT `s 1098H(2) the regime is a relevant regulatory regime` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1098H(2) the regime is a relevant regulatory regime` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1098H(5) the section that gives the meaning of "Money Laundering Regulations"` EQUALS "section 1098B(8)"
